@meghana-madhyastha @sanjayy0612 

I'm glad you're interested in LMCache, and thank you so much for your willingness to contribute to the community!

However, you can refer to the discussion in this [link](https://github.com/LMCache/LMCache/issues/3372#issuecomment-4543974808). Actually, you could look for similar issues related to f-string formatting—there are still plenty left in the codebase. You could pick one to fix as your good first issue.

(a) The engine-as-reference rule works for me. Using `Logprob.decoded_token` as-is at the inline levels and one shared resolver for standalone `/derender` keeps it to a single place that can drift, and #59241 is a good argument for settling that before the parsed path gets written. +1 to sitting the parity tests on `convert_ids_list_to_tokens` / `decode_token_id` as @shimib suggests.

(b) Agreed. Rejecting `stop` on streaming `/derender` and pointing at `output_mode=text` is the right call for now — the engine already has the hold-back, and a stateless tier rebuilding it would just be the worse copy. Agreed too that the replay cursor and any future stop hold-back should be designed together so `DerenderStreamState` changes once.

@shimib please take the parsed-path issue, I won't be able to pick it up. Happy to review it and to help with repros if that's useful.

