@holtwood Thanks, good catch. Confirmed on `1ca53a8`: the deadline check runs before `query_read_status()`, so an already-finished transfer is still reported as failed when the poll lands after the deadline.

This definitely looks worth covering with a regression test. Querying the transfer status before applying the timeout seems like a natural direction, though whether a `DONE` result first observed after the deadline should still count as success is part of the broader timeout semantics here.

If you'd like to contribute the test for this case, that would be very welcome. Otherwise I'll make sure to credit you for identifying it in the PR I'm planning for this.

Opened #5482 as a draft for the late-poll case. It queries the transfer status before applying the load deadline, so an already-terminal read is reported with its actual result.

The in-flight timeout/ownership case (A / B / C above) is intentionally unchanged and still open.

@holtwood I included an adapter-level regression test for the case you found. I left the NIXL handle-cleanup-specific test out, so if you'd still like to add that, feel free to post the test here or open a PR targeting my branch and I'll include it with credit.

